# Bidirectional file sync (see /home/scientist/.claude/plans/breezy-
# splashing-koala.md) -- runtime-generated by sync_custom_node_files, not
# something to commit even if xparo_custom_behaviors_folder_path is ever
# pointed at this source tree directly (e.g. local dev). The 8 curated
# example sources themselves (custom_behaviors/custom_node_files/{python,
# cpp,javascript,bash}/*) and examples_manifest.json are real, tracked
# files -- only the compiled/runtime byproducts below are ignored.
custom_behaviors/custom_node_files/manifest.json
custom_behaviors/custom_node_files/cpp/cpp_build/
custom_behaviors/custom_node_files/javascript/js_runtime/
custom_behaviors/custom_aiml/
custom_envs/custom_maps/

# Stress test finding F3 (LOW): engine.py's _persist_credential writes this
# robot's live ROBOT_CREDENTIAL (its auth secret for the Django server)
# here at runtime -- it was never gitignored, so a plain `git add -A` run
# from inside a real deployment's checkout could commit a live credential
# to history.
config/credential.json
